X('exporting-to-the-usa-isf-10-2',[
 ('Who files what',['The importer security filing is made by the US importer or its customs broker, not by the Indian exporter. It needs ten data items from the importer side, such as the manufacturer, the seller, the buyer, the ship-to party, the country of origin and the HTS number, and two items from the carrier. The filing is due at least 24 hours before the cargo is loaded on the vessel at the port abroad.','The exporter\'s job is to give the US importer correct and early data, because a late or wrong filing can lead to a penalty and a hold on the cargo.']),
 ('Data you will be asked for',['Name and address of the manufacturer or supplier, and of the place where the goods were stuffed.','The country of origin and the HS code, with the right description.','The container stuffing location and the consolidator, if it is a consolidated shipment.']),
 ('Planning around the 24 hours',['Fix the data before the cargo gates in, and tell the importer the exact manufacturer name and address as it appears on the commercial invoice. Changes after filing need an amendment. Ask your forwarder for the date and time by which the importer needs the information, which is earlier than the vessel cut-off.'])],
 [('Does the Indian exporter file the ISF?','Normally no. The US importer or its broker files, but the exporter must supply the data in time and correctly.')])
X('exporting-food-to-the-usa-fda-prior-notice',[
 ('Before the first shipment',['A foreign facility that makes, packs or holds food for the US must be registered with the FDA, and must name a US agent who can be contacted by the agency. The US importer has its own duties under the foreign supplier verification programme, which means the importer will ask the exporter for food safety documents and plans.','These steps take time, so start them before you agree a delivery date.']),
 ('Prior notice in practice',['The US importer or its agent sends the prior notice for each food shipment through the FDA system before the food arrives. It names the product, the manufacturer, the shipper and the arrival details. Notice must be given at least 2 hours before arrival by road, 4 hours by air or rail, and 8 hours by water. The prior notice confirmation number should be on the shipping documents.']),
 ('At the border',['The FDA can hold a shipment for examination or testing, or refuse admission if the paperwork is missing or the food does not meet the rules. Labels must meet US requirements, including allergens and the nutrition panel, and they are checked at entry. Keep the registration and the supplier records ready, since the importer will want them quickly.'])],
 [('Do small food exporters need FDA registration?','Generally yes, if the facility makes, processes, packs or holds food for consumption in the US. Some exemptions exist, so check the current rules with the FDA or an adviser.')])
X('exporting-to-the-european-union',[
 ('What the importer needs',['The EU importer needs an EORI number to make the customs declaration, and the goods are declared under a customs tariff code. The EU applies the common external tariff, so the duty is the same in every member state, but VAT is charged on import at the rate of the country of destination.','Some products need extra documents, such as a conformity marking, a health or phytosanitary certificate, or a licence, so ask the buyer what they need for your product.']),
 ('Product rules to check',['CE marking and technical files for machinery, electrical and medical products.','Chemicals rules, which require registration or authorisation for many substances.','Food and plant rules, such as limits on pesticide residues and import checks for certain products.','Packaging and labelling rules, including language and recycling requirements in some states.']),
 ('Preference and agreements',['Some Indian products have a lower duty under the generalised scheme of preferences or under other arrangements, and rules change. Ask your buyer or a customs adviser to confirm the duty and whether a preference applies at the time of shipment, because the position can change over time.'])],
 [('Who pays the VAT on goods imported into the EU?','The importer, normally, at the time of import, at the rate of the destination country. The importer can often claim it back as input VAT.')])
X('exporting-to-the-united-kingdom',[
 ('Customs and the importer',['The UK has its own customs system since it left the EU. The importer needs an EORI number starting with GB to make the declaration, or it can use an agent. Import VAT is charged on the goods at the border, and a registered importer can use a postponed accounting arrangement to account for it on its VAT return and not pay at the border.','The duty comes from the UK tariff, and the importer uses the commodity code for the goods.']),
 ('Product rules',['Many products need UKCA or CE marking, depending on the product and the date. Food and plant products need the right health or phytosanitary documents, and some have special entry points. Check the rules for your product with the buyer before you ship, since they can differ from the EU\'s.']),
 ('Trade agreement',['India and the UK have agreed a trade agreement, and whether and how it applies to a shipment depends on its entry into force and the product. Check the current position before you promise a price that depends on a lower duty, and ask the buyer\'s broker to confirm the rate on the day.'])],
 [('Do I need an EORI number to export to the UK?','The UK importer needs one to declare the goods. An Indian exporter selling DDP, or acting as importer of record, may also need one.')])
X('exporting-to-the-uae',[
 ('Duty and the agreement',['The UAE applies the common external tariff of the Gulf Cooperation Council, which is five per cent on most goods, with some goods at zero, and a few, such as alcohol and tobacco, at higher rates. Under the India-UAE Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement, many Indian products can enter at a lower or zero duty if they meet the rules of origin and carry the right certificate.','The buyer or its broker can confirm the rate for your tariff code.']),
 ('Documents for a normal shipment',['Commercial invoice, packing list and the bill of lading or airway bill.','The certificate of origin, which is needed for the preference and sometimes for other reasons.','Any product-specific certificate, such as a health certificate for food or a conformity certificate for certain goods.','The importer\'s customs registration, since the shipment is cleared against its code.']),
 ('How clearance works',['Customs clearance is done by the consignee or its agent at the port or free zone, through the local system. Goods going to a free zone may follow a different procedure, with the duty paid when the goods leave the zone into the mainland. Ask the buyer where the goods are going, because it affects the documents and the route.'])],
 [('Is the UAE a good first export market for Indian goods?','It is close, has frequent sailings and flights and has a trade agreement with India. Many exporters start there, but it is a competitive market, so check the demand and the buyer\'s standing.')])
X('exporting-to-saudi-arabia-saber',[
 ('How SABER works',['SABER is the Saudi online platform on which importers register products that fall under technical regulations. For regulated products, a product certificate of conformity is obtained before the shipment is made, and a shipment certificate of conformity is issued by an approved body for each consignment before it ships. The importer in Saudi Arabia registers and applies, and the exporter provides the test reports, the product details and the factory information.','Without the right certificate, the goods can be held at the port or refused.']),
 ('Food, drugs and cosmetics',['These fall under the food and drug authority, which has its own registration and clearance process. Products must be registered and labelled in line with local rules, often in Arabic, and the importer or the exporter\'s local agent usually handles the process. Start early, since registration can take time.']),
 ('Planning ahead',['Ask the buyer which regulation and which certificate apply to your product code.','Allow time for the tests and the certificate before you plan the shipment date.','Check that the invoice, the product name and the HS code agree with the certificate, since a mismatch can stop the clearance.'])],
 [('Do all products need SABER?','Not all, but many regulated products do. The buyer should check the list for your product before you ship.')])
X('exporting-to-nigeria-form-m-and-paar',[
 ('Form M step by step',['The Nigerian importer applies for a Form M through an authorised bank, on the trade monitoring system, before the goods are shipped. The form describes the goods, the supplier, the value and the port, and it must be approved before shipping. It is the basic import document in Nigeria and is the base for foreign exchange and customs clearance.','An Indian exporter should ask for a copy of the approved Form M before loading, and check that the details agree with the invoice.']),
 ('PAAR and the port',['After the Form M is approved, the pre-arrival assessment report is produced for the shipment. It sets out the assessed duty and is used in the customs declaration. Differences between the PAAR, the invoice and the bill of lading can lead to delays and extra assessments at the port.','Documents should reach the importer and the clearing agent well before the vessel arrives.']),
 ('Tips',['Do not ship before the Form M is approved. It can be hard to correct afterwards, and the goods may not be cleared.','Check the product against the list of goods that are restricted or prohibited for import.','Use an agent in Lagos who knows the port, because delays and extra charges are common when the paperwork is not ready.'])],
 [('Can I ship before the Form M is approved?','This is risky. Nigeria requires the Form M before shipment, and goods that arrive without a valid form can be held or refused.')])
X('exporting-to-brazil-from-india',[
 ('The importer and the system',['The Brazilian importer must be registered with the federal revenue service and be authorised to use the foreign trade system. Many imports also need a licence, which is requested through the system by the importer before shipping, and some goods need approval from other agencies, such as health or agriculture. An Indian exporter should ask the importer which approvals are needed before the order is confirmed.','A local customs broker handles the declaration, which is filed electronically.']),
 ('Taxes that add up',['Brazil charges an import duty based on the common Mercosur tariff, plus federal and state taxes on top, so the total can be much higher than the duty alone. The importer\'s adviser can work out the landed cost, and it is worth doing before you fix the price.']),
 ('Paperwork and language',['Invoices and packing lists should be clear and complete, and some documents may need translation into Portuguese. Labels on consumer goods must meet local rules. Use a forwarder with a Brazilian partner, since clearance at Santos and other ports has its own routines and charges.'])],
 [('What is the first step for a new Brazil buyer?','Ask whether the importer is registered and which licences your product needs. Then check the tariff code and the total taxes before you quote.')])
X('exporting-to-australia-biosecurity',[
 ('How the import conditions work',['Australia has strict biosecurity rules. An importer checks the import conditions for each product on the government\'s online system before the goods ship. Some goods need a permit, and others need a treatment or a certificate, such as a phytosanitary or a heat treatment certificate. The conditions depend on the product and the country, and they change.','Goods that arrive without the right paperwork can be treated, re-exported or destroyed at the owner\'s cost.']),
 ('Containers and packing',['Containers must be clean, free of soil, seeds, insects and plant matter. Wooden packaging must meet the international standard and be marked correctly, and bark and pests are not allowed. Use clean pallets and have the container inspected before loading. Some containers are inspected on arrival, and dirty ones can be ordered for cleaning.']),
 ('Customs and the agreement',['Australian importers need a business number and a broker or a self-lodged declaration. India and Australia have a trade agreement that gives lower duty on many Indian goods, with a certificate of origin. GST is charged on the import and usually claimed back by a registered importer.'])],
 [('Are Indian wooden pallets accepted in Australia?','Yes, if they are treated and marked to the international standard and are free of bark and pests. Untreated wood will be refused or treated at your cost.')])
X('shipping-cargo-to-nepal-via-india',[
 ('The transit route',['Nepal is landlocked and imports much of its sea cargo through Indian ports, mainly Kolkata with Haldia and Visakhapatnam, under the transit treaty between the two countries. The cargo moves by rail or road in bond under customs control to the border or to an inland depot in Nepal, such as the one at Birgunj, where the Nepal customs clears it.','Cargo for Nepal is not cleared for home use in India, and the Indian customs does not charge duty on it, as long as the transit rules are followed.']),
 ('Documents and conditions',['The bill of lading is made out to a Nepalese consignee, and the Nepal importer gives the documents and an import licence or approval if the product needs one. The Indian customs transit declaration is filed by a broker, and the cargo is sealed and moves under a bond or a guarantee.','The Nepalese importer needs to follow the rules of Nepal for the goods. Ask your Nepal buyer which documents are needed.']),
 ('Planning',['Plan for several steps and parties: the line, the Indian port, the rail or road operator, the border and the Nepal agent. Allow extra days for the border, and check the free days at each point, since delays at the border can raise detention charges.','Cargo from India to Nepal, which is a normal export, is a different case and follows the usual export process.'])],
 [('Does cargo for Nepal pay Indian customs duty?','Cargo moving in transit to Nepal under the treaty does not pay Indian duty if it follows the transit rules. Nepal charges its own duty on arrival.')])
